 {
  "text": "Luiz, it's Megan from the regional office. Two things before Thursday. Rezende Agro has been overdue since March, so that is five months now, and this morning they asked us for another sixty days. Second, I have looked at their file. They have bought from us for eleven years, and this is the first season with a problem. So I am not saying no. I am saying I want your read before I answer them. Call me back today.",
  "voice": "ellen",
  "file": "a2_listening1.mp3"
 },
 {
  "text": "Mister da Silva, this is Paulo Rezende at Rezende Agro. I have tried to reach you twice this week, so I am leaving a message instead. I have owned this store since two thousand and six, and in twenty years I have not asked a supplier for more time. I am asking now. My soybean truck has been at the port for nine days, and the buyer has not paid me for that load. I do not want a bigger limit. I want sixty days, and I am sending you the port document today.",
  "voice": "arthur",
  "file": "a2_listening2.mp3"
 },
